<%# Every stream tab on the profile empties out into the same centred shape the
    rest of the client uses - a glyph over a heading and a line naming what will
    fill the tab - rather than a bare sentence sitting in a list row, which
    reads as a row that failed to render. The words differ per tab because what
    fills a tab differs: a Likes list fills when the account reacts to a post, a
    Media grid when it attaches one. Locals: `glyph`, `heading`, `note`. %>
<div class="empty-state">
  <span class="empty-state-icon" aria-hidden="true"><%= icon(glyph) %></span>
  <h2><%= heading %></h2>
  <p><%= note %></p>
</div>
